we are taken into the Islamic states  last stronghold after a final night of  heavy bombardment this is where the  so-called Caliphate ended as we enter  the center of bagus the convoy stops  there's still one area of resistance a  militant Mattoon come on swatter ban SDF  forces move us back whilst the last  blows are delivered  we're still hearing the sporadic sound  of gunfire the last pocket of is it's  just over there  but what we're witnessing are the final  moments of the Islamic state this is a  significant victory for the Syrian  democratic forces and it has taken a  long time in coming but although is is  defeated on the battlefield this isn't  the end of the group it's likely now to  go underground and fight a guerrilla  insurgency eventually the guns do fall  silence and we journey into a dark  apocalyptic hellscape corpse is rotting  in the pallid spring Sun the stench is  everywhere blown on the desert winds  it is an unbelievable sight a wasteland  this is where the Islamic state made its  last standard a junkyard encampment you  can see in the distance bedsheets and  costs that have been erected as tents  there's more over here and you can see  how the fighters work we're living these  tunnels and foxholes under here which  would help them evade the bombardment  from the coalition jets and artillery  but this is really all that now is left  of what once was the Islamic state for  the Kurdish forces this victory is  traced with sadness many died as martyrs  in what was a global fight the future of  their people is also far from secure it  is why the declaration is a surreal  moment an understated ceremony on a  rooftop overlooking the Euphrates River  the commander who led the fight  confirming Isis's rule is over  [Music]  the road to the end of the Islamic state  is a journey through destroyed  communities town after battered town  tells a story of years of fighting to  break the group's poisonous stranglehold  on Iraq and Syria what comes next will  depend on whether there can be effective  government and how these regions are  reconstructed whilst the victory is  complete there are still areas that need  searching for Isis fighters more often  than not the soldiers tasked with the  duty are shooting at shadows the ghosts  of Isis will haunt these places for a  long time to come the desperation and  the inglorious final stand of the group  though is hugely damaging to its brand  but even with its flag in tatters it  still has the resources to rise up from  this and strike again
 

